From 481427cf3273cc61b1decb9277fb6f5bef6937cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: w07 <w07@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:53:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rootsuite): leave a test's output log where its siblings
 read it

RootTestDriver.cmake writes what it judges to <build>/<testname>.log, and
roottest's tests read that file by name: reference seds the log schemaRun1
left in the directory, and every schemaRun*check diffs its sed against
<build>/reference.log. The harness judged the output in memory and wrote no
log at all, so those four checks died on 'sed: schemaRun1.log: No such file'
with a fixture that had in fact been set up.

The plan now gives each roottest test its log path (plan.log_file, the
directory being the working copy's mirror of CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR) and
judging writes the compared output there - empty for a test that checks only
stderr, as the driver's  is. An OUTREF naming <build>/x is resolved to
x, which discovery recorded as 'dir/<build>/dir/x' before, and read from the
working copy when a test produced it there.

roottest/root/treeformula/schemaEvolution: 5 FAIL -> PASS (reference,
schemaRun2check, schemaRun2acheck, schemaRun4check, schemaRun4acheck); the
two schemaRun3* checks stay UNSUPPORTED for xrdroot's missing TTreeFormula.
No PASS lost over roottest/root/treeformula/* (163 tests).
